Tomcat Setup 1st Way
====================

Launch amazon Linux 2023 and install tomcat manually first and then automatically using script

All apache software are available in http://dlcdn.apache.org --> tomcat --> tomcat-11--> v11.0.27--> bin--> apache-tomcat-11.0.27.tar.gz

Step1: install java
-------------------
dnf install java-21-amazon-corretto -y

Step 2: download tomcat
----------------------
yum install -y wget

wget https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-11/v11.0.27/bin/apache-tomcat-11.0.27.tar.gz

Step3: Extract
--------------
tar -zxvf apache-tomcat-11.0.27.tar.gz

Step4: Configure user, passwords and roles
-------------------------------------------
 --> cd apache-tomcat-11.0.27/conf/
 --> vi tomcat-users.xml
     Add new files --> copy 3 lines and paste, line 56
     <role rolename="manager-gui"/>
     <role rolename="manager-script"/>
     <user username="tomcat" password="raj@123" roles="manager-gui,manager-script"/>

Step 5: Delete line 21 and 22 -- if not delete, we need to give public ip
------------------------------
  --> cd apache-tomcat-11.0.27/webapps/manager/META-INF
  --> vi context.xml

Step 6: Start Tomcat
--------------------
  --> cd apache-tomcat-11.0.27/bin
  --> sh startup.sh

Connection
==========
http://IP:8080
manager apps --> username: tomcat, password: root123

